     "parsed_output": null,
     "text": "Same 4096-element tile per block as the best candidate, plus two small hints. I don't have a measurement for this combination yet, so expect it to land about level with 0.0216 ms. I chose it because every earlier variant clustered within noise of that time.\n\n- **Tile and grid:** one 4096-element fp16 tile per block, giving a grid of 5120 blocks.\n- **Static length:** the array length is fixed at compile time. Since 20971520 is a multiple of 4096, the compiler can see that every tile is fully in bounds. If the length were not a multiple, the last partial tile would still be padded on load and clipped on store.\n- **Load hint:** both input loads carry `latency=10`, telling the compiler the reads come from DRAM so it can issue them as early as possible.\n- **TMA:** left to the compiler's default. Round 7 forced it off and timed the same as round 3.\n\nBandwidth estimate:\n\n- **Traffic:** each call moves 120 MiB, made of two 40 MiB reads and one 40 MiB write.\n- **Ceiling:** at the 8 TB/s vendor figure the floor is about 15.7 \u00b5s.\n- **Current:** 21.6 \u00b5s is about 5.8 TB/s, so the remaining gap is likely mostly launch overhead and practical bandwidth limits rather than the mapping.\n\n```python title=\"impl_cutile.py\"\nfrom typing import Annotated\n\nimport torch\nimport cuda.tile as ct\n\nConstInt = ct.Constant[int]\n\n# Fixed configuration literals\n_TILE = 4096          # elements per block (fp16 -> 8 KiB per input tile)\n_LOAD_LATENCY = 10    # DRAM-traffic hint for the streaming input loads\n_STATIC_SHAPE = True  # array length baked in as a compile-time constant\n\n_CONFIG = {\"TILE\": _TILE, \"LOAD_LATENCY\": _LOAD_LATENCY, \"STATIC_SHAPE\": _STATIC_SHAPE}\n\n# 1-D array whose length is a compile-time constant: with n a multiple of TILE\n# the compiler can prove every tile is fully in bounds; otherwise the last\n# partial tile is still bounds-handled (padded load / clipped store).\nStaticVec = Annotated[\n    ct.Array,\n    ct.ArrayAnnotation(index_dtype=ct.int64, static_shape_dims=(0,)),\n]\n\n\n@ct.kernel\ndef _vector_add_kernel(x: StaticVec, y: StaticVec, out: StaticVec,\n                       TILE: ConstInt, LAT: ConstInt):\n    bid = ct.bid(0)\n    a = ct.load(x, (bid,), (TILE,), latency=LAT)\n    b = ct.load(y, (bid,), (TILE,), latency=LAT)\n    # Bounds-clipped store drops any lanes past n in a partial last tile.\n    ct.store(out, (bid,), a + b)\n\n\ndef run(x, y):\n    xf = x.view(-1)\n    yf = y.view(-1)\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    of = out.view(-1)\n    n = xf.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    grid = (ct.cdiv(n, _TILE),)\n    ct.launch(torch.cuda.current_stream(), grid, _vector_add_kernel,\n              (xf, yf, of, _TILE, _LOAD_LATENCY))\n    return out\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_CONFIG)\n```",
